<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>R</m> is the region where <m>x \le 6</m>, <m>y \lt 4</m> and <m>7x + 5y \ge 35</m>. For each point, choose where it is.</p><ol><li><div><m>({5}, {4})</m> [ inside R | on an edge of R, included | on an edge of R, not included | outside R ]  </div></li><li><div><m>({-3}, {4})</m> [ inside R | on an edge of R, included | on an edge of R, not included | outside R ]  </div></li><li><div><m>({4}, {3})</m> [ inside R | on an edge of R, included | on an edge of R, not included | outside R ]  </div></li><li><div><m>({6}, {0})</m> [ inside R | on an edge of R, included | on an edge of R, not included | outside R ]  </div></li></ol></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Substitute each point into all three inequalities. A point is in <m>R</m> only if it makes every inequality true. A point on a solid edge belongs to <m>R</m>; a point on a dashed edge does not. A point can be on one of the lines and still be outside <m>R</m>.</p><ol><li><p><m>({5}, {4})</m>: <m>5 \le 6</m>, <m>4 \lt 4</m>, <m>55 \ge 35</m>. It is on the dashed line <m>y = 4</m>, which is not included: on an edge, not included.</p></li><li><p><m>({-3}, {4})</m>: <m>-3 \le 6</m>, <m>4 \lt 4</m>, <m>-1 \ge 35</m>. It is on the line <m>y = 4</m>, but <m>y \lt 4</m> is false: outside <m>R</m>.</p></li><li><p><m>({4}, {3})</m>: <m>4 \le 6</m>, <m>3 \lt 4</m>, <m>43 \ge 35</m>. All three are true and the point is on no line: inside <m>R</m>.</p></li><li><p><m>({6}, {0})</m>: <m>6 \le 6</m>, <m>0 \lt 4</m>, <m>42 \ge 35</m>. It is on the solid line <m>x = 6</m> and satisfies all three: on an edge, included.</p></li></ol></p></solution>
    <answer><p>on an edge of R, not included</p></answer>
    <answer><p>outside R</p></answer>
    <answer><p>inside R</p></answer>
    <answer><p>on an edge of R, included</p></answer>
</stack-static>